RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-15T12:35:08.3711580Z Note: a multi-user installation is possible. See https://nix.dev/manual/nix/stable/installation/installing-binary.html#multi-user-installation
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-15T12:35:08.3720035Z ^[[1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer^[[0m
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-15T12:35:08.3797628Z ^[[32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-15T12:35:08.3805660Z ^[[0m
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-15T12:35:08.3805962Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-15T12:35:08.3806414Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-15T12:35:08.3806525Z 
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-15T12:35:08.3806624Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-15T12:35:08.3806870Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-15T12:35:08.3807061Z 
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-15T12:35:08.3807198Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-15T12:35:08.3807488Z    if you are ready to continue.
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-15T12:35:08.3807622Z 
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-15T12:35:08.3807935Z 3. Create the system users ^[[34m(uids [30001..30008])^[[0m and groups ^[[34m(gid 30000)^[[0m
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-15T12:35:08.3808251Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-15T12:35:08.3808529Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-15T12:35:08.3808715Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-15T12:35:08.3808801Z 
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-15T12:35:08.3808883Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-15T12:35:08.3809011Z 
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-15T12:35:08.3809107Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-15T12:35:08.3809300Z    can use Nix.
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-15T12:35:08.3809369Z 
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-15T12:35:08.3809419Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-15T12:35:08.3809496Z 
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-15T12:35:08.3809765Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-15T12:35:08.3810126Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-15T12:35:08.3815459Z 
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-15T12:35:08.3815787Z I will:
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-15T12:35:08.3816025Z 
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-15T12:35:08.3816315Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-15T12:35:08.3816763Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-15T12:35:08.3817225Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-15T12:35:08.3817645Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-15T12:35:08.3817971Z  - install Nix in /nix
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-15T12:35:08.3818292Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-15T12:35:08.3818732Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-15T12:35:08.3819159Z    /root
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-15T12:35:08.3826858Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-15T12:35:08.3827462Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-15T12:35:08.3836120Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-15T12:35:08.3836384Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-15T12:35:08.3836522Z 
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-15T12:35:08.3837899Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mReady to continue?
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-15T12:35:08.3838176Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-15T12:35:08.3851553Z 
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-15T12:35:08.3852034Z ^[[34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-15T12:35:08.3859722Z ^[[0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-15T12:35:08.3860108Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-15T12:35:08.3860396Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-15T12:35:08.3860574Z 
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-15T12:35:08.3860689Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-15T12:35:08.3860871Z 
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-15T12:35:08.3861017Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
